def subsystems():
    S = O('subsystems.json'); rt = O('rtti_foc.json')
    L = ['# Engine subsystem map (StarWarsG.exe FoC x64)', '',
         'Generated by `tools/re/subsystems.py` + `make_docs.py`. Class lists come from RTTI (`rtti_classes.txt`); grouping is rule-based on class '
         'names (verify borderline cases). Entry points are functions referencing `Class::Method` diagnostic strings (exact RVAs, usable as '
         'breakpoints/xrefs). Address locality (`tools/re/locality.py`) attributes un-named functions to the nearest named TU.', '',
         '## Archive mounting, EaW fallback and Lua loading (answers for the assets stream)', '',
         'Source: disassembly of the boot function at **0x5d990** (it also sets fonts, registry `Software\\Petroglyph`, etc.), '
         '`MegaFileManagerClass::Add_Megafile` **0x216b50**, MegaFiles.xml loader **0x217740**, EaW-locator **0x21dce0**.', '',
         '**(b) EaW GameData fallback - yes.** 0x21dce0 locates the base game and logs `Setting FALLBACK_PATH to %s`: it tries the registry '
         '(`Software\\LucasArts\\Star Wars Empire At War\\1.0` -> `ExePath`, checks `Revision`), then `..\\..\\EAW\\Run\\` (LaunchSWEAW.bat layout), '
         'then **`..\\GameData\\`** (Steam layout, checks `..\\GameData\\sweaw.exe`). A `FALLBACKPATH=` command-line switch overrides it. '
         'If no EaW install is found FoC aborts with `Unable to locate the installation path of Star Wars: Empire At War...`. '
         'The fallback path (global std::string at RVA 0xa15320) is then used to mount EaW\'s archives first.', '',
         '**(a) Mount order** (as executed in 0x5d990):', '',
         '1. if FALLBACK_PATH set: `<EaW>\\Data\\MegaFiles.xml` (every listed .meg, in file order)',
         '2. `<EaW>\\Data\\Patch.meg`, `<EaW>\\Data\\patch2.meg`, `<EaW>\\Data\\64Patch.meg` (each only if present)',
         '3. `.\\Data\\MegaFiles.xml` (FoC, in file order)',
         '4. `Data\\Patch.meg`, `Data\\patch2.meg`, `Data\\64Patch.meg` (FoC; hard-coded strings at 0x802db8/0x802dc8/0x802dd8, not in MegaFiles.xml)',
         '5. FALLBACK_PATH registered as a secondary loose-file root (call 0x214110).', '',
         '`Add_Megafile` assigns each archive an incrementing load index and **inserts it at the head of the archive list** (push_front), so lookup '
         'walks newest-first: **later mounts override earlier ones**. Effective priority, highest first: FoC 64Patch > FoC patch2 > FoC Patch > '
         'FoC MegaFiles.xml entries (last listed wins) > EaW 64Patch > EaW patch2 > EaW Patch > EaW MegaFiles.xml entries. Loose files on disk '
         '(and `MODPATH=`/`STEAMMOD=` mod directories, parsed at 0x67d70; `RELAUNCH MODPATH=Mods/%s`) take precedence over archives in FileClass '
         'open; exact loose-vs-meg ordering for the FoC dir vs FALLBACK dir should be confirmed dynamically (one breakpoint on 0x216b50 and on the '
         'file-open path). Audio megs (`SFX2D_<LANG>.meg`, `SFX2D_Non_Localized.meg`, `SFX3D_Non_Localized.Meg`) are opened separately by the SFX '
         'managers, not through MegaFiles.xml.', '',
         '**(c) Lua loading.** Lua 5.0.2 is linked in with both parser and undumper; `lua_load` auto-detects precompiled chunks by the `\\033Lua` '
         'header, so the engine accepts source **and** bytecode. Bytecode must match the VM (`virtual machine mismatch in %s: size of %s is %d but read %d` '
         'on size_t/Instruction/lua_Number) - the x64 build therefore cannot load the retail 32-bit bytecode in config.meg, and 64Patch.meg overrides '
         'them with text sources (consistent with the assets worker\'s finding). Scripts are resolved by name under fixed roots '
         '(`.\\Data\\Scripts\\AI\\`, `AI\\SpaceMode\\`, `AI\\LandMode\\`, `AI\\StoryArc\\`, `Interventions\\`, `Evaluators\\`, `GameObject\\` + `.lua`), '
         'AI dirs are enumerated with `*.lua` (0x4e7e30); `require` uses `LUA_PATH` (default `./?.lua;./?.lc`). Errors: `LuaScript Error in %s.lua!` '
         '(0x246af2). Files are read through the MegaFile/FileClass layer, so loose `Data\\Scripts` files (mods) override archived ones.', '',
         '**(3) Effects.** All rendering goes through the D3DX9 Effects framework: `D3DXCreateEffectPool` (shared parameters), `D3DXCreateEffect` '
         '(from compiled .fxo in memory), `D3DXCreateEffectCompilerFromFileA` (dev path for .fx source), and a custom `ID3DXEffectStateManager` '
         '(alD3dEffectStateManager) + `ID3DXInclude` (alD3dIncludeHandler). Engine-provided parameters are bound by **semantic/annotation name** through '
         'alD3d*EngineParam classes (e.g. `_EngineParam_Get_D3d_Model_Transform`, fog, FOW texture/UV, sphere-harmonic lights `alD3dSphLightAllParam`, '
         'time, wind bend, shadow extrusion, resolution constants). A port needs: (1) an fx_2_0 bytecode -> HLSL/SPIR-V path (or the original .fx '
         'sources from the mod tools), (2) a re-implementation of the engine-param semantic table, (3) the technique/pass model (Begin/BeginPass/'
         'CommitChanges ~30M calls in the prior patch\'s probe CSV -> per-draw effect state is the dominant CPU render cost).', '',
         '## Threading model (as shipped)', '',
         'Single simulation+render thread (MainThreadClass). Extra threads only via ThreadClass (0x22e490 -> CreateThread 0x786138): '
         'LoadingThreadClass (load screen), network PacketHandler/NAT threads, BattleLoadDialog. Pools use `EmptyLockerClass` (no locks). '
         'Intel TBB is shipped but unused. So every subsystem below currently runs serially in the frame.', '']
    order = ['simulation_core', 'gameobject_behaviors', 'physics_collision', 'pathfinding_movement', 'ai_planning', 'ai_perception', 'combat_targeting',
             'abilities', 'lua_script', 'story', 'renderer', 'audio', 'ui', 'networking', 'file_io', 'memory', 'misc']
    L += ['## Summary', '', '| subsystem | RTTI classes | named entry points |', '|---|---|---|']
    for s in order: L.append(f"| {s} | {len(S[s]['classes'])} | {len(S[s]['entry_points'])} |")
    for s in order:
        v = S[s]
        L += ['', f'## {s}', '']
        if s in SUB_NOTES: L += [SUB_NOTES[s], '']
        cls = [c for c in v['classes'] if not c['name'].startswith(('std::', 'DynamicVectorClass', 'LuaMemberFunctionWrapper', 'PooledObjectClass', 'EventFactoryClass', 'codecvt', 'num_', 'money', 'time_', 'collate', 'ctype', 'messages', '_Mpunct', 'numpunct'))]
        if s == 'memory':
            tmpl = collections.Counter(c['name'].split('<')[0] for c in v['classes'])
            L.append('Template instantiations: ' + ', '.join(f'{k} x{n}' for k, n in tmpl.most_common(12)) + '\n')
            cls = [c for c in cls if '<' not in c['name']]
        L.append('Key classes (name `vtable`(slots) <- parent): ' + ', '.join(
            f"{c['name']} `{c['vtable']}`({c['slots']})" + (f" <- {c['parent']}" if c.get('parent') else '') for c in cls[:160]))
        if v['entry_points']:
            L += ['', 'Entry points (Class::Method -> function RVAs):', '']
            for e in v['entry_points'][:80]:
                L.append(f"- `{e['class']}::{e['method']}` {', '.join(e['functions'])}")
    open(D('SUBSYSTEMS.md'), 'w').write('\n'.join(L) + '\n')

